"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2946,"**
Narrated to us Abu Bishr al-Wasiti: Narrated to us Khalid ibn 'Abdullah, from Khalid, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to the *Saqayah* (a water-dispensing place) and asked for a drink. Al-'Abbas (RA) said, ""O Fadl, go to your mother and bring the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) a drink from her.""

So he brought it, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Give it to me to drink."" Al-'Abbas (RA) said, ""O Messenger of Allah, they have put their hands in it."" He (ﷺ) said, ""Give it to me to drink."" So he drank from it.

Then he (ﷺ) came to Zamzam, where they were giving water and working at it. He (ﷺ) said, ""Work, for indeed you are upon righteous work."" Then he (ﷺ) said, ""Were it not that you would be overpowered, I would pull up the rope until I placed it upon my shoulder,"" meaning his own shoulder, and he pointed to his shoulder.

Abu Bakr (RA) said, ""This is of the type which we say: Indeed, a gesture stands in place of speech."""
